f we change the color of this  we can effectively tint it whatever  color we want  but by default  let's stick with white which turns it  off  next let's do saturation  so i'm gonna use a lerp node  hold l left click alright and we want to  kind of slide between  a saturated version  of our texture and that's what we set up  here so i'll take this multiply into b  and i want to slide between this and a  desaturated version and i'm just going  to pull one of these color channels  because they are black and white by  default  right into a and we can hold s  make a parameter  i'll call this saturation  plug that into the alpha  and at default if i plug this into base  color now  right 0 gives us a black and white image  20 gives us something really saturated  and 1 is default that's exactly what we  want and finally let's set up a  brightness control very very simple a  multiply node  hold m and left click  we'll pipe this in  all the way through  and hold s  for a parameter  i'll call this brightness  plug right into b  and by default it's set to zero it's  gonna just be  total darkness  one gets us a normal looking effect and  20  totally maxes it out  so that's about it the only thing we  need to do is right click this color  node here and convert it to a parameter  we'll call it tint  and we can select all this hit c  title it albedo and we're almost done i  just want to have control over the  specular and roughness channels of our  material as well so i'll right click  specular  bring that out right click roughness  that's good to go  and i'll stick to the qixel mega scans  defaults specular they usually do 0.5  roughness of one  and that should do it i'll save close  out and we can right click our master  material and create a material instance  which we can apply to  our 3d mesh right here  boom wonderful two things i want to do  setup wise i'll double click  the actual  scan itself  and i'm going to apply  this material instance to it  so by default it just comes out with  this material and i want to adjust a  couple of these parameters in the  material instance  so let's give it a slightly warmer tint  and i want to give it a bit more normal  intensity so i'll set that to about  three and that feels pretty good  to me  bam we got ourselves  a solid photo scan here  this is pretty good for like mid-ground  background kind of scans the closer you  get with your drone to the actual  mountain the higher res your 3d mesh  will be  thank you so much for watching i hope  you all learned something new in this  video and are getting inspired to do  your own 3d scans it's a blast and it's  such a cool way to start collecting your  own asset library of unique custom  assets  if you want to get your hands on these  photo scans i do have them uploaded to  my patreon otherwise you can download  the processed images i have of one of  the scans and run it in reality capture  yourself  good luck and happy scanning see you  guys next week  [Music]  you
 

